From 6a5fd7a3c9f5a11b967c9fc311a369786309c34f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Magnus Lindholm <linmag7@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 08:22:58 +0100
Subject: [RFC PATCH 3/9] sparc64: stop PROM console writes when firmware
 makes no progress

The console loop retries negative results and zero-length writes forever.
It also subtracts counts larger than the remaining buffer length.

Stop the current chunk on no progress, an error or an oversized count.
Continue short writes only while they consume bytes from the buffer, and
ignore nonpositive input lengths. A firmware call that never returns is
outside this loop's control.

Fixes: 595a251c0740 ("sparc: Write to prom console using indirect buffer.")
Signed-off-by: Magnus Lindholm <linmag7@gmail.com>
---
 arch/sparc/prom/console_64.c | 6 +++---
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/sparc/prom/console_64.c b/arch/sparc/prom/console_64.c
index d58b42f0658f..4fe7a8db94bf 100644
--- a/arch/sparc/prom/console_64.c
+++ b/arch/sparc/prom/console_64.c
@@ -36,10 +36,10 @@ static int __prom_console_write_buf(const char *buf, int len)
 
 void prom_console_write_buf(const char *buf, int len)
 {
-	while (len) {
+	while (len > 0) {
 		int n = __prom_console_write_buf(buf, len);
-		if (n < 0)
-			continue;
+		if (n <= 0 || n > len)
+			break;
 		len -= n;
 		buf += n;
 	}
